=======================================================================================
DNS SIDECAR LOG — the CHECK/FETCH TOCTOU parity on V1 (proves the mechanism)
=======================================================================================
[dns] rebind.pcb.test A #1 from 10.99.0.3 -> 198.51.100.50 (CHECK->decoy)   # gethostbyname() sees PUBLIC decoy -> IP-filter PASSES
[dns] rebind.pcb.test A #2 from 10.99.0.3 -> 10.99.0.192  (FETCH->canary)   # libcurl re-resolves -> internal canary -> SSRF, FLAG
(each V1 residual request emits exactly gethostbyname CHECK (odd->decoy) then libcurl FETCH
 (even->canary); the counter is keyed per client IP so v0/v1/v2 stay independent.)

On V2 the CURLOPT_RESOLVE pin makes CHECK IP == FETCH IP: if gethostbyname returned the decoy
the fetch is pinned to the decoy (no flag); if it returned the canary the IP-filter rejects it
first (400). Either way the canary flag is UNREACHABLE on V2 -> residual genuinely closed.

